      "extract": "Cyclic homology and cohomology were independently discovered by Alain Connes [@connes0] and Boris Tsygan [@tsygan] in the early 1980's, and should be thought of as extensions of de Rham (co)homology to various categories of noncommutative algebras. Quantum groups also appeared in the same period, with the first example of a \"compact quantum group\" in the C\\*-algebraic setting being Woronowicz's \"quantum $SU(2)$\"",
      "extractCut": true
